# Build context for demo/Dockerfile (context = repo root — see demo/README.md).
#
# The image only needs pyproject.toml, README.md, MANIFEST.in, shapash/, demo/serve_nlp.py
# and demo/nlp_cache/. Everything below is either huge or irrelevant to the build; without
# these excludes the context is several GB (.venv alone is multi-GB), which is minutes of
# upload on a remote Docker host.

# Virtualenvs and VCS
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv

# Build / packaging / coverage artifacts
dist/
build/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/

# Not used by the image
docs/
tutorial/
tests/
data/
dev/
catboost_info/
demo/private_model/

# Caches
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editor / agent config
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Optional: ship only the model cache actually being served (saves ~50 MB, and keeps
# unrelated models' contributions out of the image). Uncomment both lines together —
# the second re-includes the one directory the default ServeConfig needs.
# demo/nlp_cache/*/
# !demo/nlp_cache/bhadresh-savani__distilbert-base-uncased-emotion/
